# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Technical documentation and audit working files.
#
# The sibling ITC project excludes documentation/ wholesale. That keeps the
# repository small and makes it unbuildable: render_site.mjs reads the registry,
# so a fresh clone can re-render the site only on the machine that built it. The
# published pages survive because problems/*.qmd are committed, but nothing can
# regenerate them, and the evidence behind every verdict lives only on one disk.
#
# So the directory is excluded by default with deliberate exceptions, in two
# groups: the small inputs the site build needs, and the judgments that cannot
# be recomputed.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so each level
# is excluded by its contents (dir/*) and the next level down re-included, all
# the way to the files that are kept.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
documentation/*
!documentation/audit/
documentation/audit/*
!documentation/audit/calibration.json
!documentation/audit/seed-citations.json
!documentation/audit/seed-citation-map.json
!documentation/audit/registry/
!documentation/audit/canonical/
!documentation/audit/schema/
documentation/audit/registry/*
!documentation/audit/registry/problems.json
!documentation/audit/registry/human-queue.json
documentation/audit/canonical/*
!documentation/audit/canonical/problems.json
documentation/audit/schema/*
!documentation/audit/schema/*.json

# Everything below is a judgment made once and written down. The seed extraction is one
# reading of the source document; an opinion is one auditor's assessment of one entry; a
# synthesis file is the rewrite that survived that assessment; a reading finding is one
# paper read in full with a verbatim quote; a review verdict is one external model's
# judgment on a claim that would change the registry. None of it can be regenerated:
# re-running the external auditors returns different text, and re-reading 573 papers is
# the cost of the whole reading phase. This is the same rule the screening decisions are
# kept under, and for the same reason.
!documentation/audit/raw/
documentation/audit/raw/*
!documentation/audit/raw/*.json
!documentation/audit/opinions/
documentation/audit/opinions/*
!documentation/audit/opinions/*.json
!documentation/audit/synthesis/
documentation/audit/synthesis/*
!documentation/audit/synthesis/*.json
!documentation/audit/reading/
documentation/audit/reading/*
!documentation/audit/reading/findings/
documentation/audit/reading/findings/*
!documentation/audit/reading/findings/*.json
!documentation/audit/reading/QUOTE-CHECK.md
!documentation/audit/reading/review/
documentation/audit/reading/review/*
!documentation/audit/reading/review/verdict-*.json
# One labeller's reading of what a gap is an instance of, and the record of which
# absences more than one labeller named. The payloads regenerate from the findings;
# these do not, and UNCOVERED.md is the only place the labellers' closing reports
# survive at all.
!documentation/audit/reading/gaps/
documentation/audit/reading/gaps/*
!documentation/audit/reading/gaps/themes.json
!documentation/audit/reading/gaps/labels/
documentation/audit/reading/gaps/labels/*
!documentation/audit/reading/gaps/labels/*.json
!documentation/audit/reading/UNCOVERED.md
!documentation/audit/reading/uncovered/
documentation/audit/reading/uncovered/*
!documentation/audit/reading/uncovered/out/
documentation/audit/reading/uncovered/out/*
!documentation/audit/reading/uncovered/out/*.json
!documentation/audit/auditors/
documentation/audit/auditors/*
!documentation/audit/auditors/*/
documentation/audit/auditors/*/*
!documentation/audit/auditors/*/out/
documentation/audit/auditors/*/out/*
!documentation/audit/auditors/*/out/*.json

# The study program's judgments. A triage verdict is one model's decision about
# whether a problem is studiable and by what design; a design is its ADEMP
# protocol for one of them. Re-running either returns different text, which is
# the same reason the auditor opinions are kept, and the reports are the only
# form either is readable in. The prompts and the raw CLI transcripts beside
# them are regenerable and large, and are not kept.
!documentation/studies/
documentation/studies/*
!documentation/studies/DESIGNS.md
!documentation/studies/REVIEWS.md
!documentation/studies/verify/
documentation/studies/verify/*
!documentation/studies/verify/*.json
!documentation/studies/triage/
documentation/studies/triage/*
!documentation/studies/triage/verdict_*.json
!documentation/studies/triage/QUEUE.md
!documentation/studies/designs/
documentation/studies/designs/*
!documentation/studies/designs/*-design.json
!documentation/studies/designs/*-critique.json
!documentation/studies/designs/*-revised.json
# Proposed designs for problems the queue excluded; written once, like a design.
!documentation/studies/proposals/
documentation/studies/proposals/*
!documentation/studies/proposals/*.md

# The screening decisions. Everything else under refs/ is regenerable: the corpus comes back
# from a search, the batches from the corpus, the PDFs from their identifiers. A decision is
# a judgment made once about one record and there is nowhere to fetch it from again, so it is
# the one thing here that must survive losing this disk.
!documentation/refs/
documentation/refs/*
!documentation/refs/systematic/
documentation/refs/systematic/*
!documentation/refs/systematic/screening/
documentation/refs/systematic/screening/*
!documentation/refs/systematic/screening/decisions.jsonl
!documentation/refs/systematic/screening/index.json
!documentation/refs/systematic/search-log.json

# Quarto render output and caches
/docs/
/_site/
/.quarto/
*_files/
/site_libs/
**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Per-file HTML left in the source tree by an interrupted Quarto render
/*.html
/problems/*.html
/categories/*.html

# R
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
*.rds

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node (site build script)
node_modules/

# Agent guidance files. ITC ignores CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and .claude/ entirely,
# which leaves the agent definitions that produced the reading unrecorded. The
# house style and the reading protocol are what make the prose one voice, so
# they are tracked here; only local agent settings are not.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/*.md

# Working directories the reading agents extract paper text into. Regenerable
# from the PDFs and large enough to dominate the repository.
/scratch/
/scratchpad/

# Simulation study working files, for the study queue triaged from the finished
# registry. Raw per-replicate output is regenerable from the master seed and
# large; the tracked artifacts are the analysis outputs under results/*.csv and
# the rendered manuscripts, which are what the manuscript reads.
/studies/*/results/raw/
# Enumerated truth, cached per scenario so a two-hour run resumes. Small, but
# regenerable from the master seed like the replicates beside it; the tracked
# artifact is results/truth.csv, which the analysis and the manuscript read.
/studies/*/results/truth-cache/
/studies/*/results/pilot/
/studies/*/results/cells/
/studies/*/results/smoke-cells/
/studies/*/logs/
/studies/*/manuscript/manuscript_files/
/studies/*/manuscript/*.md
/studies/*/manuscript/*.pdf
/studies/*/manuscript/*.odt

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Run driver logs; the results they produce are what is tracked.
/studies/*/results/drive.log
/studies/*/results/drive.pid
/studies/*/results/replication/drive.log
/studies/*/results/*.log
